      "text": "To simplify the expression \\((x^5 + x^4 + x + 10) - (x^5 + 2x^4 - x^3 + 12)\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Distribute the negative sign through the second polynomial.\n2. Combine like terms.\n\nLet's start by distributing the negative sign:\n\n\\[\n(x^5 + x^4 + x + 10) - (x^5 + 2x^4 - x^3 + 12) = x^5 + x^4 + x + 10 - x^5 - 2x^4 + x^3 - 12\n\\]\n\nNow, we can combine like terms:\n\n\\[\nx^5 - x^5 + x^4 - 2x^4 + x^3 + x - 12 + 10\n\\]\n\nSimplify each group of like terms:\n\n\\[\n(1 - 2)x^4 + x^3 + (1 - 12)x + (10 - 12)\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n-x^4 + x^3 - 11x - 2\n\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-x^4 + x^3 - 11x - 2}\n\\]\n\nTo ensure the accuracy of our result, let's verify it using Python code.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, simplify\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the expressions\r\nexpr1 = x**5 + x**4 + x + 10\r\nexpr2 = x**5 + 2*x**4 - x**3 + 12\r\n\r\n# Simplify the difference\r\nsimplified_expr = simplify(expr1 - expr2)\r\n\r\nprint(simplified_expr)\n```",
